    "turn_id": "d09_final_matched:r2:t1",
    "narration": "Iris sits on one of the simple stools beside the nearer bed, her weight settled, hands resting in her lap. The floor around them is quiet — bare wood, two empty wardrobes, two empty cabinets, nothing yet to fill the space with purpose. She looks across at Nicco.\n\n\"I don't know what makes it comfortable yet,\" she says. \"We've only just started.\" A beat passes. \"But asking helps.\"\n\nShe doesn't elaborate or rush to fill the silence after that, letting the plainness of the room and the question sit between them.",
